Cell["6. Cancellation-factor families and boundary closures", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9f750526-13c2-4e7f-b3a6-dfe58d11a626"],

Cell["\<\
Across the 8 staged candidates, the number of cancellation factors per \
candidate has profile <|6 -> 2, 2 -> 5, 5 -> 1|>. Part I returns one \
generator per candidate; in these samples each generator factors into two of \
the reported cancellation factors. After canonicalising overall signs and \
normalisations, there are 18 distinct cancellation-factor polynomials and 6 \
distinct product generators. The identity of the factor set or generator is \
therefore a useful family label; the factor count alone need not be.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b9e17bd3-ebe3-4252-b15f-5898a9c33480"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"factorGroups", "=", 
   RowBox[{"GatherBy", "[", 
    RowBox[{"factorRecords", ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"#1", "[", "\"\<FactorKey\>\"", "]"}], "&"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"generatorGroups", "=", 
   RowBox[{"GatherBy", "[", 
    RowBox[{"generatorRecords", ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"#1", "[", "\"\<GeneratorKey\>\"", "]"}], "&"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"KeyTake", "[", 
   RowBox[{"auditSummary", ",", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<DistinctCancellationFactorCount\>\"", 
      ",", "\"\<DistinctGeneratorCount\>\"", 
      ",", "\"\<PullbackVectorsSharedAcrossGeneratorFamilies\>\"", 
      ",", "\"\<BoundaryVectorsWithInteriorExtension\>\"", 
      ",", "\"\<BoundaryVectorsWithoutInteriorExtension\>\""}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:=",ExpressionUUID->"abe4cf59-e978-4aec-b9e0-0136df5bb213"],

